  "finding": "For the corpus/agentic prompt the budget optimum declines modestly with context (argmax 7@2K -> 5@32K -> 4@126K) but the curve is flat near the peak: budget 3-5 sit within ~0.5 tok/s at 2K/32K, and budget 4 is at/near the peak at every context and the clear optimum at 126K (19.27 tok/s). Budgets 6-7 regress at length as acceptance falls and ms/cycle rises. The short-context preference for high budget is acceptance-driven, not a generalizable context effect: the natural mtpbench suite peaks at budget 4 (acceptance ~0.49), while the high-acceptance merge prompt peaks at 7. The \u00a711.1 prediction that the optimum RISES with context after #1 is falsified (it flat-to-falls). The shipping default candidate_budget=4 is the robust measured choice (general-suite optimum at short context, universal optimum at long context); a static context->budget map gives no generalizable gain, so no runtime policy/flag is added. The genuine adaptive lever is acceptance/profit-based online depth adaptation (follow-up).",
  "correctness": "exact=True for every budget at every context (DFlash IDs == true AR)",
  "tool": "scripts/muse_glimmer_dflash_context_budget_sweep.py"
}